cursesdemo-by-dc5 (1.0+1-0ddebs8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changes prepared with Claude Opus 5.5
  * debian/control : rewrote the description, recommend mpg123
  * debian/control : new cursesdemo-by-dc5-data package with the
    soundtrack (patchbay.mp3), which was not installed
  * debian/copyright : upstream author (Aaron J. Grier, tfinn),
    Octothorp for the soundtrack, full text of the GPL-2+ license for
    debian/*
  * debian/patches/01_adapt_makefile.patch : honour CPPFLAGS (fortify),
    drop -ltermcap (alias of libtinfo)
  * debian/patches/02_fix_terminal_handling.patch : restore the terminal
    at the end (endwin), take the terminal size from curses, draw the
    missing "5" sprite, fix the compiler warnings
  * debian/patches/03_play_soundtrack.patch : play the soundtrack with
    mpg123, new --no-music option
  * debian/patches : DEP-3 headers completed (Forwarded)
  * debian/resources/cursesdemo-by-dc5.png : the icon was an empty file
  * debian/resources/cursesdemo-by-dc5.desktop : run in a terminal,
    added Keywords and a French comment, dropped the matching lintian
    override
  * debian/*.lintian-overrides : commented the overrides, added the
    pandoc groff-message override
  * debian/cursesdemo-by-dc5.6.md : documented the demo, its option and
    the soundtrack, regenerated the manual page

 -- Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:59:55 +0100

